---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Stackchan — Greg O\'Brien" current={0}>
<div data-screen-label="Work case study">
<div style="border-top:1px solid var(--edge);margin-top:38px;padding:40px 56px 0">
<a href="/build" style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none;transition:color .2s ease" class="h-ink">← All work</a>
</div>
<div style="padding:34px 56px 44px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">
<div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted)">Personal · Hardware</div>
<h1 style="margin:18px 0 0;font-family:Newsreader,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:54px;line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;max-width:22ch">Stackchan</h1>
<p style="margin:18px 0 0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.65;max-width:46ch;color:var(--body)">An ESP32 desktop companion robot, currently getting taught to have opinions — an experiment in giving an LLM a face and a personality.</p>
</div>
<div style="padding:40px 56px 24px"><div style="border:1px solid var(--edge)"><div data-shot="1" style="height:260px;background:var(--tileA);display:flex;align-items:flex-end;padding:20px"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--tileAInk);letter-spacing:.08em">[ PROJECT SCREEN OR PHOTO ]</span></div></div></div>
<div data-split="1" style="padding:0 56px 44px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:56px;align-items:start">
<div>
<div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)">The problem</div>
<p style="margin:18px 0 0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--body);max-width:70ch">I wanted something on my desk that felt less like a chatbot window and more like a small creature with opinions. Most AI demos live inside a browser tab — I wanted to see if giving one a face, a body, and a fixed personality changed how it felt to talk to, even though the underlying model was the same one anyone could get from an API.</p>
<div style="margin-top:34px;font-size:17px;font-weight:600">What I did</div>
<p style="margin:9px 0 0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--body);max-width:70ch">Stackchan started as an ESP32 board with a small screen for a face, built on an open hardware pattern originally designed for smart-speaker style projects. I wired it up to a language model, gave it a name and a personality brief instead of a generic assistant prompt, and started teaching it to hold opinions instead of hedging every answer.</p>
<div style="margin-top:26px;font-size:17px;font-weight:600">How it works</div>
<p style="margin:9px 0 0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--body);max-width:70ch">The ESP32 handles the face — expressions, a bit of movement — while the actual thinking happens through an LLM call. The personality lives in the prompt, not the hardware: consistent opinions, a few running jokes, and instructions to disagree with me occasionally instead of being endlessly agreeable.</p>
<div style="margin-top:26px;border:1px dashed var(--dash)"><div data-shot="1" style="height:190px;background:var(--stripe);display:flex;align-items:flex-end;padding:20px"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted);letter-spacing:.08em">[ DIAGRAM OR SCREEN ]</span></div></div>
<div style="margin-top:34px;font-family:Newsreader,serif;font-size:25px;line-height:1.25;max-width:52ch">"It’s amazing how much personality changes when you take an assistant that’s designed to hedge and just tell it: pick a side."</div>
<div style="margin-top:34px;font-size:17px;font-weight:600">Where it stands</div>
<p style="margin:9px 0 0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--body);max-width:70ch">Still very much a work in progress. Right now it’s better at holding a consistent personality than at being useful for anything in particular — which is honestly the more interesting problem to me at the moment.</p>
</div>
<div style="border:1px solid var(--edge);padding:26px;background:var(--surface)">
<div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)">Detail</div>
<div style="margin-top:16px;display:flex;flex-direction:column">
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:84px 1fr;gap:18px;padding:11px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ruleSoft);font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--body)"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)">Status</span><span>In progress</span></div>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:84px 1fr;gap:18px;padding:11px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ruleSoft);font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--body)"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)">Built with</span><span>ESP32, a small OLED face, an LLM for personality</span></div>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:84px 1fr;gap:18px;padding:11px 0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--body)"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)">Timeframe</span><span>2026 — ongoing</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:40px 56px 14px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline">
<span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)">Next</span>
<a href="/build" style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none;transition:color .2s ease" class="h-ink">All work →</a>
</div>
<div style="padding:14px 56px 44px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--muted)">More write-ups coming as new projects are finished.</div>
</div>
</Layout>
